WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:03.140
Hey, good murning!

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.650
Karen, you're saying it like that on purpose, aren't you?

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.320
Karen-chan, good murning.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.610
Murning.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.650
Everyone in Class A is doing it!

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.700
I made it popular.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.950
These things become habits, you know.

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.250
Things like "murning"...

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:20.660
Good morning, everyone.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:23.350
Sensei, good murning.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.880
Good morning, everyone.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:29.380
Morning.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.960
Morning.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:32.550
What's wrong?

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.640
Good morning, Alice.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:40.390
What's going on?

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:43.020
Alice is against saying "murning".

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.770
<i>What beautiful Japanese.</i>

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.370
Shino...

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.410
Happy birthday.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.040
What?

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:25.700
It's today, right?

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.080
Yes, thank you.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.000
Seriously?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.380
I thought it was coming up...

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.590
Here.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:35.760
You can have this juice.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:37.490
Thank you.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.770
I don't have anything to give you, so I'll sing you a song.

00:02:47.770 --> 00:02:48.560
A song?

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:52.560
Birthday, you.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:59.740
Birthday, you, Shino.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.390
Birthday, you.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:06.990
Birthday, you, Shino.

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.920
How old do I look?

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.630
Like a high school student.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.420
I mean, what age do I look like?

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.720
Well, you were in middle school until just recently, so 14 or 15?

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.550
But I wouldn't be surprised if she told me she was 30!

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.680
She has a certain calmness about her.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.760
Huh?

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.520
Youko, how could you say that?

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.700
It's hopeless, Alice.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.360
I simply don't act young enough.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.440
That's not true, Shino.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:38.610
What's going on?

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.240
This morning...

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.320
<i>It's your birthday today, isn't it?</i>

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:45.950
<i>Yes.</i>

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:46.950
<i>What?</i>

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>Happy birthday.</i>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.710
<i>You're 36 this year, right?</i>

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:51.830
<i>No!</i>

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.250
<i>Shino, is that true?</i>

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.130
<i>No!</i>

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.040
<i>You're so mean, Onee-chan.</i>

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.840
<i>Sorry, but you don't act young at all.</i>

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.320
<i>If you'd told me, I would've gotten you a present.</i>

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.720
<i>I forgot all about it myself.</i>

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.560
<i>A present?</i>

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.770
<i>I'll get you the perfect present.</i>

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:12.850
<i>Like what?</i>

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.270
<i>A bonsai tree?</i>

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.860
<i>I'm not an old woman!</i>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:19.900
That's what happened?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.440
A bonsai tree's pretty harsh.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.410
But bonsai trees are very valuable.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.030
I'm jealous.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.370
I don't want a bonsai tree.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.410
Anyway, what does "not acting young enough" actually mean?

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:33.370
Well, it means...

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.330
You're old.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.670
I'm not old!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:39.590
I wonder if I'm young enough.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.050
You're really young.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.420
You don't even look like a high school student.

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:45.330
Hooray.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.850
Maybe it's because of the way you talk.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:52.100
You always speak formally to everyone.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.250
I see.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.010
I'll try speaking more casually.

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.400
Like a high school girl!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.900
Ya know how tall the Eiffel Tower is?

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:04.530
I heard it's, like, 324 metres tall.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:05.500
Really?

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:06.280
No way!

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.230
Like that?

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:09.660
That's not quite it.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.620
Your older sister sounds more like a high school girl than you do...

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.660
Though, I guess she is one.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.000
You've got the same blood in your veins.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.830
Maybe you could be a model, too.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:23.670
But my sister takes after my mother, and I take after my father.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.470
Okay, let's do a photo shoot!

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.510
Shino, you sit there.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.970
Okay.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.520
Upsy-daisy.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.230
Is something wrong?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.020
But if you do a photo shoot, you have to wear a swimsuit.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.020
Why?

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.860
Isn't that what they do in gravure shoots?

00:05:41.860 --> 00:05:44.290
My sister's a fashion model.

00:05:44.290 --> 00:05:45.820
She doesn't wear swimsuits.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.150
Damn.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.070
Damn?

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:52.080
I like seeing the curves of a woman's body.

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.830
Aya, if you took your clothes off, I bet you'd...

00:05:55.540 --> 00:05:57.960
Y-You pervert!

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.180
Huh?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:00.790
Why?

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.590
Nice smile.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:04.300
Yeah.

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.300
But she could never be a model.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:12.600
I wish I could give you something more substantial.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:13.770
It's all right.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:15.310
It's the thought that counts.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:20.830
I couldn't ask for a better present than spending my time with you.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.740
Shino...

00:06:24.520 --> 00:06:27.350
But if you insist on giving me something,

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.660
I'd take a strand of your hair.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.160
You're scaring me!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.080
I bought you a present.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.550
Really?

00:06:37.550 --> 00:06:38.910
Thank you.

00:06:42.040 --> 00:06:43.670
A snow globe.

00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:44.590
Can I really have this?

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:45.880
It looks expensive.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:47.800
I got it from a 100 yen shop.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.880
It's well-made for the price!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:50.800
Here, I got something for you, too.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:52.140
A bonsai tree!

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:53.680
It's fake.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.370
Can I really have this?

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.100
It's not even my birthday.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.690
I bought it because I thought you'd like it.

00:06:59.690 --> 00:07:01.600
Isami, thank you.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.350
My, my.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.100
Huh?

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:07.320
She stole Alice from you?

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:10.070
I don't stand a chance against my sister.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.080
Shino, do you have a computer?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.000
My sister has a laptop.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.210
But computers have viruses, so she won't let me touch it.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.720
What?

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.980
Are you gonna get sick if you touch it?

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.050
Really?!

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.480
That's what my sister says.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.230
C-Can you?

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.980
Youko, calm down.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:45.090
<i>If we gave Shino a computer...</i>

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.230
Pictures of blonde girls!

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:49.980
Amazing.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:54.520
My folder of blonde girls is full of dreams and gold!

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:58.810
<i>Well done, Isami-san.</i>

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.760
<i>She knows exactly how to handle her.</i>

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:10.340
I wonder if Shino will like it.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:11.630
Of course she will.

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.430
I wonder if they're sisters.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:15.010
They're so cute.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:19.350
People always mistake us for sisters in Japan.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.240
Probably because you're so small.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.400
We don't look the same age at all.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.020
What are you talking about?

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:27.480
I'm the older sister.

00:08:27.480 --> 00:08:29.780
No, you're the younger sister.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:32.110
No, I'm the older sister.

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:33.610
You're the little sister.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:34.490
The older sister.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:35.410
Little sister!

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:36.490
Older sister!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:42.660
I think everyone would agree that Alice looks like the younger of the two.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:44.880
You're right.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:47.670
She looks like a cute little sister.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.840
The whole world's little sister...

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.170
The whole world's?

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:52.050
See?

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.380
You're the younger sister.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:58.970
But you used to follow me around, crying your eyes out!

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:07.350
<i>Alice.</i>

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.170
You've grown so much!

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.450
Alice, I'll-

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:24.300
It's all right.

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:25.710
I can get it myself.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:28.210
I mean, you can sit on my shoulders.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:31.340
Now you can get it.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.880
Careful! Careful!

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:34.590
Which book?

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.340
The third from the right.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:38.860
Oh, okay.

00:09:38.860 --> 00:09:40.850
You can go on ahead.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.560
Aya, are you having trouble reaching?

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:48.440
<i>Did I trigger a "sit on her shoulders" flag?</i>

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.480
I can get it myself.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.490
I don't need to sit on your shoulders.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:55.900
My shoulders?

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:00.120
In English, both older and younger sisters are just called "sisters".

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:01.030
That's right.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.660
Maybe it's a cultural difference.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:04.870
People aren't so concerned with age.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:05.790
Really?

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.500
Well, between the two of you,

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.460
Alice is definitely the younger sister.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.540
I keep telling you, I'm the older sister.

00:10:12.830 --> 00:10:13.560
What?

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.630
But you just said you aren't concerned with age.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:18.010
I'm the older sister.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:20.840
Alice, teach me how to do this.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:21.700
Sure.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:22.720
Which subject?

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.100
English.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:26.060
What?!

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:29.270
Oh, s-sorry.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.650
19 points...

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:36.280
I've gotten so used to Japanese, my English is suffering.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.570
Karen, you have all the answers right.

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:41.660
You just wrote them in the wrong order.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.280
You're so smart, Alice.

00:10:44.280 --> 00:10:47.020
You got 100 on our last test.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.870
That's amazing!

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.880
<i>My grades are better.</i>

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.710
Karen, we got the same score.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.970
Shino, we made the same mistakes.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.200
So we did.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.480
Alice, when are we going to give them to her?

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.770
Oh, right.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:18.240
We bought you a present yesterday, Shino.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.790
It's a birthday present.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.910
Why, thank you!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.990
I got you a fan.

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.270
How wonderful.

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:29.120
I bought you foreign stamps.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:33.350
Karen, how did you know what I wanted?

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:34.670
You must be psychic!

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:36.600
<i>It's not fair.</i>

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.790
<i>I'm not psychic.</i>

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.800
I'm sorry for getting so excited.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:44.640
Alice?

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.850
Shino, do you like Karen more?

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:48.990
What?

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:49.930
Um...

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.170
Huh?

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:52.850
What?

00:11:52.850 --> 00:11:54.150
What kind of battlefield is this?

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.820
Look at that face!

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:01.530
She's in the eye of the storm!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.870
Alice, are you still upset about this morning?

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.990
I don't mind being the little sister.

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:09.620
T-That's not the problem.

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:13.830
You shouldn't fight.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:17.340
Alice is Alice, and Karen is Karen.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.420
Everyone is good in their own way.

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:25.050
Karen, I know you followed Alice to Japan,

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:28.760
and I know you like Karen, Alice.

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:30.350
Shino.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.650
<i>That's it...</i>

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:49.030
<i>I was jealous of them.</i>

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.920
I like you, Shino, but I like Karen just as much.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:58.250
Alice, I love you, too.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.920
I love, love, love you too, Shino.

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.590
That's too many "loves"!

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:04.430
What?

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.290
You're such good friends, you even fight with each other.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:14.840
Alice-san!

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.280
Karen-san!

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.900
Your relationship seems a little strained recently,

00:13:22.900 --> 00:13:24.860
so I made a soothing gift for you.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:25.990
Here.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:32.410
We've already made up.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.000
Oh, my.

00:13:45.520 --> 00:13:48.510
Can I share your textbook?

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:49.700
Sure.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.520
<i>What beautiful blonde hair.</i>

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.940
<i>And she's so close.</i>

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:05.570
<i>I wonder if this is some kind of foreign skinship.</i>

00:14:06.700 --> 00:14:07.700
Karen-chan.

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.700
<i>Oh yeah, there was something I wanted to tell Alice.</i>

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.030
<i>I'll go talk to her after class.</i>

00:14:17.870 --> 00:14:20.080
<i>I'm not sure I'll remember it by the end of class.</i>

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:20.840
<i>I know!</i>

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.090
<i>I'll write it down.</i>

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.670
Class is over.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:32.940
I need to go see Alice.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:37.350
<i>Seaweed boiled in soy sauce?</i>

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:46.610
Are you sure you're all right?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:50.070
My mother's here, so I'll be fine.

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:50.710
Go on.

00:14:50.710 --> 00:14:53.460
Everyone's waiting.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.520
See you later.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:15:00.370
Make sure you say hello to Matsuki-san from next door if you run into her.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.930
She did seem a little under the weather.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:22.690
Really? I wanted to take the day off and look after her.

00:15:22.690 --> 00:15:24.560
She went to the hospital, right?

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:26.820
She'll be fine with a day's rest.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.820
B-But when I think about if something happens to her while I'm at school...

00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:32.240
You worry too much.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.290
Aya, what do we do?! Listen to this!

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:36.430
Spring has arrived!

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:37.950
Yippee!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:38.610
What's wrong with you?

00:15:38.610 --> 00:15:39.500
Do you have a fever?

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.000
Take a look at this.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:43.580
A letter?

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.240
You idiot!

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:45.500
Keep your voice down.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:47.630
It was in my shoe locker.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:48.510
Is this a love-

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.590
Not so loud!

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.970
Shut up.

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:54.260
Wow, is that a love letter?

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.140
Nice pronunciation.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.350
A love letter?

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.750
That's great, Youko.

00:15:58.750 --> 00:16:00.060
You're so popular.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.270
Popular?

00:16:01.270 --> 00:16:04.190
You're making me blush.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.980
<i>What does "popular" mean?</i>

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:10.500
<i>Is it similar to palpable?</i>

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.610
<i>Oh, it must be.</i>

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.240
That's great, Youko.

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:16.070
You're so palpable.

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:17.700
<i>Is that supposed to be a compliment?</i>

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.580
You haven't looked inside yet, have you?

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.410
You don't actually know if it's a love letter.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.080
What?

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:24.500
But it was in my shoe locker!

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:27.380
Is there any other reason someone would write a letter?

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.840
There are plenty of reasons.

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.540
Like what?

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:34.470
It could contain grave news.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:37.440
You must burn that letter immediately.

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:38.720
That's just an example.

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:42.770
In any case, we'll know what it is once we've opened it.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:44.730
Aya, don't.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.860
The letter is addressed to Youko.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:49.480
You can't just read it.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:52.380
You're right.

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:54.030
I'm sorry.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.110
I'll read it by myself later.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:16:59.580
You can let go now.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:03.120
<i>So curious, so curious, so curious!</i>

00:17:07.380 --> 00:17:09.630
Stare...

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:13.630
Stare...

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.760
Stare...

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:25.020
What?

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:26.130
Can I help you?

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.400
Who is the love letter from?

00:17:28.790 --> 00:17:30.980
Oh, I haven't looked yet.

00:17:30.980 --> 00:17:32.190
Hurry up and look at it!

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:34.570
There's no name on it.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:37.130
It may be from a girl.

00:17:37.130 --> 00:17:42.160
I'd imagine you'd be more popular with girls than boys.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:45.410
I've got a feminine side!

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:48.920
When we were playing baseball in P.E. the other day,

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:51.340
I twisted my foot when I slid into base.

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.380
So what?

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.280
It shows I'm delicate!

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.970
I don't think delicate girls slide into base.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:01.220
I guess I need to be more ladylike.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.720
You're not the ladylike type.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:08.060
Aya, you're pretty ladylike and girly.

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:09.500
Yes, that's it!

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.070
I'll try acting like Aya!

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:20.990
You dropped your mechanical pencil.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:22.940
T-Thanks.

00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:23.650
It's fine.

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:24.790
Don't mention it.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.580
Let's both study hard.

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.750
I don't act like that!

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:31.260
What?

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:33.210
I think that was pretty accurate.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:38.340
<i>Youko still hasn't made any attempt to read the letter.</i>

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.140
<i>When is she going to read it?</i>

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:44.140
<i>How Youko chooses to respond isn't my business,</i>

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.600
<i>but why do I feel like this?</i>

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:49.570
Komichi-san, could you read this section?

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:52.400
I don't understand.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:54.230
I don't understand anything!

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.110
What's wrong, Komichi-san?

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.700
Aya, let's go home.

00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:03.260
Huh?

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:04.160
What about your letter?

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:05.530
Letter?

00:19:05.530 --> 00:19:07.410
Oh, I forgot.

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.250
What?

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:11.210
There might be something important written in there,

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.670
so I guess I should read it.

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:20.050
C-Congratulations.

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:21.410
On what?

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.180
I think you've got the wrong idea.

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:24.100
Huh?

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:25.720
I'm happy to have received the letter,

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.760
but I always meant to turn them down.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:28.520
Why?

00:19:28.880 --> 00:19:31.230
Because no matter who wrote it,

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.330
I like you more.

00:19:36.250 --> 00:19:38.030
Just open it already.

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:40.130
What are you talking about?

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:43.520
I was just saying how great it is to have friends.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.280
Okay, I'm going to read it.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:47.830
"How are you doing?"

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.160
"It's Shinobu."

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.100
"How is England?"

00:19:51.100 --> 00:19:53.250
"The weather in Japan is nice."

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.710
"Alice is so energetic and small."

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:56.590
"I'll write again soon."

00:19:58.050 --> 00:19:59.630
"Please translate all this into English."

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.050
What is this?

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:04.470
I wanted to talk to Alice's parents,

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:08.890
so I wrote a letter, figuring I'd ask Alice to translate it for me.

00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:12.440
I thought it might seem like a love letter if I put it in her shoe locker.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.980
It was in mine...

00:20:14.300 --> 00:20:15.830
Oh, my.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.770
Youko-chan, did it excite you?

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.840
It was a disappointment.

00:20:19.840 --> 00:20:20.650
What?

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:24.660
She sounded better.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.160
I hope she can come to school tomorrow.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:27.950
Yeah.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:29.870
It's so boring without her.

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:34.120
She really had us wrapped around her finger today with that prank, though.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.420
But everything worked out.

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:39.710
Now that I think about it, there's no way you'd receive a love letter.

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.380
What did you say?!

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:43.630
Ayaya's in a good mood.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:45.180
I wonder why.

00:20:45.180 --> 00:20:45.470
You seemed pretty interested in that letter.
I wonder why.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:48.470
You seemed pretty interested in that letter.

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:28.450
Bye.

00:22:28.750 --> 00:22:30.340
See you tomorrow.

00:22:35.120 --> 00:22:36.540
See you later.

00:22:45.050 --> 00:22:48.380
I greeted people on my way to school and back.

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:53.890
<i>G-Good morning.</i>

00:22:58.940 --> 00:23:01.060
<i>Goodbye!</i>

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:02.690
That's good.

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:07.180
I was worried whether you'd be all right on your own.

00:23:07.180 --> 00:23:12.330
It was fine, but I like being with you more.

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:19.430
Good night.

00:23:21.580 --> 00:23:23.110
Youko, are you sick, too?

00:23:23.110 --> 00:23:24.510
Maybe a little.

00:23:24.510 --> 00:23:25.110
Wait.

00:23:25.110 --> 00:23:26.690
I have some medicine somewhere...

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:29.750
<i>This isn't cold medicine.</i>

00:23:29.750 --> 00:23:31.000
How's your head feeling?

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.730
What do you mean by that?!

00:23:32.730 --> 00:23:34.140
See you next time.

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:34.850
Later.
